Jacob the Priest ascended today, November 19th, 2006.  The priest 
ascension has been the most difficult for me, and I've probably gone 
through 100-200 priests, although most of these were before I had the 
experience of my first ascension.  I had two versions of the Jacob the 
Priest that got pretty far, but both of them died from cockatrice-related 
deaths.

I got Excalibur early on by dipping in a fountain.  The Minetown priest 
was co-aligned, a plus.  The Quest was easy--there were tons of undead, 
but they were all sleeping, and I was able to dispatch them one at a time 
(perhaps because I was stealthy).  The Quest was also a treasure trove, 
with many chests and large boxes.  I got several new spellbooks this way, 
although no spellbook of identify.

My pet died fairly early on.  He had first stepped on a polymorph trap and 
had turned into a baby gray dragon, quickly becoming a gray dragon.  Soon 
after, I foolishly left out a chameleon corpse, and my dragon ate it, 
turning into a very weak fox, who survived for maybe 50 more turns.

I got my first wish by sitting on a throne.  I decided to make things much
easier by wishing for blessed +2 GDSM.  After this point, I wasn't as
careful about searching for traps and stepped on a few polymorph traps,
not a problem.

At the Castle, a soldier with a wand of lightning zapped me, causing some 
of my rings to explode, including my ring of digestion.  Rather annoying.  
I did find another at a later point though.

Once I had the Wand of Wishing, I only used one wish, for a blessed
spellbook of polymorph.  At best, I only had about a 48% chance of casting 
the spell, but I used the spell to gain various useful items, including a 
spellbook of identify.

At one point in Gehennom, Jacob was hungry, and instead of eating a fresh 
body on the same square, I wasn't paying attention, and he instead ate an 
unfresh soldier corpse.  Besides making him sick, it also gained him the 
aggravate monster intrinsic.

The Wizard of Yendor appeared quite a few times.  At Moloch's Sanctum, he 
appeared to be chatting with the high priest, because he spent the entire 
time in the sanctum and didn't come after me while I was battling my way 
through the corridors.

The elemental planes were easy.  On the Astral Plane, I decided to go on a
rampage, and I killed off most of the monsters, including each of the
riders several times.  It certainly helped that my AC was -53 (would go up
to -57 if I cast protection).  While on the Astral Plane, I got both
Magicbane and Giantslayer after killing two stranded adventurers.  
Eventually, I tired of this, and offered the AoY:

You offer the Amulet of Yendor to Lugh...
An invisible choir sings, and you are bathed in radiance...
The voice of Lugh rings out: "Congratulations, mortal!"
"In return for thy service, I grant thee the gift of immortatility!"
You ascend to the status of Demigod...

